      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T20:15:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK...in that case my reading of the guidelines is the opposite:\n\nIn short:\n\nUse devicetree to describe hardware and its boot-time configuration. Examples include peripherals on a board, boot-time clock frequencies, interrupt lines, etc.\n\nUse Kconfig to configure software support to build into the final image. Examples include whether to add networking support, which drivers are needed by the application, etc.\n\n\n\nSo I think this is clearly boot-time config and not software support.",
      "parentUuid": "d6eed96f_16863b02",
      "revId": "7a5587939ea7f2370b999bedbba3b8d52421994e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "672ab086_578cf143",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T20:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The EC and it\u0027s console channel system is entirely software.\n\nJust because this describes the way those console channels are at boot does not make it hardware configuration.\n\nThe console channels enabled by default is by no means a property of the mainboard and it\u0027s layout...",
      "parentUuid": "abaf14d8_48aeed3b",
      "revId": "7a5587939ea7f2370b999bedbba3b8d52421994e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11507122_768fc3e7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T20:20:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you are confused by \"boot-time\" here.\n\nThis is referring to *hardware* boot-time properties, such as clock frequencies. EC console channels still aren\u0027t hardware properties.",
      "parentUuid": "672ab086_578cf143",
      "revId": "7a5587939ea7f2370b999bedbba3b8d52421994e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50116a48_32e6d9d0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T20:25:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I stand by this...we can chat about it later if time.\n\nThe doc is silent on this case, in fact. It says what devicetree is for and what Kconfig is for (selecting which code is built), but not how to deal with something which does not affect which code is built and is not config for a physical hardware device.\n\nAnyway, arguably the console is a mux device with virtual channels, which could be implemented in s/w or h/w...\n\nI think there is pollution coming over from Linux here, where they try very hard to have static data tables in the image instead of using devicetree for config. In U-Boot, devicetree is used for config.",
      "parentUuid": "11507122_768fc3e7",
      "revId": "7a5587939ea7f2370b999bedbba3b8d52421994e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
